# ── Private key material ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backup PRIVATE key must never enter the repository. Its whole purpose
# is to live somewhere the production host cannot reach, so that a compromised
# host cannot decrypt its own offsite snapshots — committing it here would
# hand it to anyone with clone access and to every CI runner.
#
# `backup-privkey.asc` was tracked (empty) and sat waiting for someone to paste
# a key into it; one `git add -A` later it would have been in the history.
# The PUBLIC key is deliberately NOT ignored: it belongs on every backup-
# producing host and is safe to distribute.
*.asc
!backup-pubkey.gpg
backup-privkey*
*.privkey
*-private.gpg
secring.*

# ── Dotfiles: deny by default ────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything beginning with a dot is ignored, and the handful this repo
# genuinely needs is re-admitted by name below.
#
# The inversion is deliberate. A dotfile is where a secret lands by default —
# .env, .env.local, .npmrc with a token, a stray .pem — and the previous
# approach was a list of the ones we had thought of. That list is only ever as
# good as the last person's memory, and it is one `git add -A` away from being
# wrong; the empty `backup-privkey.asc` sitting tracked in this repo is what
# that looks like when it nearly happens. Deny-by-default fails the other way:
# a new dotfile is invisible until someone deliberately un-ignores it.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. `.*` sits above every negation because git takes the LAST
# matching pattern, so anything re-admitted must appear after it — including
# the `!.env.example` further up this file, which is repeated below for
# exactly that reason.
#
# This does NOT un-publish anything. .gitignore governs untracked files only;
# a file already committed stays tracked and stays on GitHub until it is
# explicitly removed with `git rm --cached`.
.*

# Repository infrastructure — CI, hooks, toolchain pins.
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep
!.github/
!.husky/
!.nvmrc
!.lintstagedrc.mjs
!.dockerignore
!.vercelignore
!.eslintrc.js
!.terraform.lock.hcl

# Env TEMPLATES only. A real .env stays ignored by the rule above — these are
# the documented shape of one, with no values in them.
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# `.claude/` is NOT re-admitted. Agent definitions, skills and launch config
# are local tooling, not part of the product, and they were the only tracked
# dotfolder that could be untracked without breaking something: `.github/`
# carries every CI and deploy pipeline, `.husky/` the pre-commit hook. Removed
# from the index on 2026-08-26; the files stay on disk.
